{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/462500-confused-by-anchors","id":462500,"title":"Confused by Anchors.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T11:37:13-07:00","id":462500,"title":"Confused by Anchors.","content":"I've been reading through Vampire 2.0 and I just can't figure out the Anchors.<br /> The Mask is what you show humanity, or it is the fa\u00e7ade you put on, or something.<br /> The Dirge is what you are around vampires, or how you really are underneath, or something else.<br /> The Touchstone is the person that reminds you of humanity and is very useful for keeping humanity and not frenzy. You lose it and you either find a replacement or get Languid before falling into Torpor. Do you wake up languid?<br /> I just need help figuring these out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:07:30-07:00","id":462551,"title":"","content":"what isn't clicking for you on Mask &amp; Dirge?<br /> <br /> You wake up, seek out a Touchstone, and if you don't find one/don't look for one, you probably wind up Languid again. Surely your character must care about <i>something</i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:26:26-07:00","id":462631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/462500-confused-by-anchors#post462500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading through Vampire 2.0 and I just can't figure out the Anchors.<br /> The Mask is what you show humanity, or it is the fa\u00e7ade you put on, or something.<br /> The Dirge is what you are around vampires, or how you really are underneath, or something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mask and Dirge are the vampire equivalent of Virtue and Vice. Like Virtue and Vice, they reaffirm the character's sense of identity, and restore Willpower as a result.<br /> <br /> Mask is, in general terms, how you act within human society. So you chose one of the Archetypes (or make up your own) to describe who your character pretends to be in mixed company, a conceit to the Masquerade. Then when you take the actions described in the archetype in order to protect that false identity, you regain the appropriate amount of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Dirge is how you act around other vampires. Again, you chose an Archetype, and when you take the actions described in the archetype in defense of the identity you use within the Danse Macabre, you regain Willpower accordingly.<br /> <br /> Neither necessarily have to be your &quot;true self&quot; or your &quot;fa\u00e7ade&quot; - they could easily both be artificial, or both be genuine aspects of your personality. It's more about who you are in what company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/462500-confused-by-anchors#post462500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Touchstone is the person that reminds you of humanity and is very useful for keeping humanity and not frenzy. You lose it and you either find a replacement or get Languid before falling into Torpor. Do you wake up languid?<br /> I just need help figuring these out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Youve got the general idea. A Touchstone is a tie to humanity, whether that be a person, a place, an object, or even a habit or routine. Most often, they are people. They protect your Humanity because they remind you of who you used to be, and what it was like to be human. They can help talk you down from Frenzy by reassuring you that you once had a conscience instead of a Beast, and you can still chose to listen to it. If you lose your last Touchstone (note that this is not the same as having your last Touchstone detached - losing a touchstone only happens when the person dies, or your relationship with them is otherwise irrevocably damaged), you've just lost the last thing connecting you to the mortal world. Most likely, the only living person you still see as anything more than cattle. You no longer have any real reason to rise from the grave each night, there is nothing left for you in the world of the living. If you don't find a new reason to go on living soon, you're likely to just give up and remain a corpse. If you decide, after a few decades, to try this whole undead thing again, you'll still need to find a new reason to go on un-living, and you'll still need to find it before your ennui sets back in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-30-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}